#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179450 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8332e831-fb93-567f-ae21-a80716a57f70" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Negative Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "66ce7121-0e0c-5108-86c4-3c11f4434b5e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12963" :question/problem "Calculate $(-9 ) \\cdot (-5).$" :question/worked-solution "We have a product of two negative numbers, $\\color{red}-9$ and ${\\color{red}-5}.$ So the product will be positive:\n![](images/17/1793b9f5cb618eb1fe60e0ea34ce271a42e44ca04e92d7546289239fffee2a40.svg)\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $9$ and $5$ without any signs: $9 \\cdot 5 = 45.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-9)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)} = {\\color{blue}45}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33b32ea7-dd7d-5e41-8fdb-142ec9da82c8" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying More Than Two Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "ce77ea1c-ff60-5548-abdf-d64e23574943" :question/math-academy-id "e-12965" :question/problem "What is the value of $(-3) \\cdot (-5) \\cdot (-10)?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of two negatives, which gives a positive: \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-3)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)} = {\\color{blue}15}.\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{\\color{red}(-3)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)}}_{\\large {\\color{blue}15}} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)} = {\\color{blue}15} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)}.\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that a positive times a negative gives a negative:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}15} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)} = {\\color{red}-(15\\cdot 10)} = {\\color{red}-150}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179452 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "192eeaef-4283-5db1-9a8f-0f2fbff163d1" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "741da5ab-8c69-5eff-af12-3fbadc2d9fb4" :question/math-academy-id "e-12966" :question/problem "Calculate ![](images/5b/5bc84ed7352b634beafa94e49a471b572e749307630e34e1e6f24a3c9ba2e177.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We have a product of two negative numbers, so the product will be positive, and we can drop the minus signs as follows:\n![](images/76/7687ac2259cb4c0e43ef7899fba49d37133444905fdde539e6278cbdf7a5c81a.svg)\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n![](images/1c/1cb412aef30a8b0dda2368ea1d8529fc3c5ba33a263e909ac1f476a47502c116.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179453 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179824 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e39bc3f9-6e7c-5e13-abe1-ba7d88c68379" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Decimals"}] :question/id #uuid "375a9118-9e3c-5fda-b787-5f3012296150" :question/math-academy-id "e-12968" :question/problem "What is $(-3.4) \\cdot 3.8?$" :question/worked-solution "We have the product of a negative number and a positive number, which gives a negative number.\n\n$$\n(-3.4) \\cdot 3.8 = -(3.4 \\cdot 3.8) = -12.92\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8332e831-fb93-567f-ae21-a80716a57f70" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Negative Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14efa79e-dbf8-502c-8685-8bcd5f506991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442342} {:answer/id #uuid "1c834ffa-bbdb-500f-b598-a17b2fa8e179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442345} {:answer/id #uuid "a33340b6-9e1a-58fb-9042-0f5a650eed0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id